From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahnaf Shahriar <ahnaf.shahriar@neuralink.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NRF52840_Timer: Add shortcuts, BitMode, capture fix, and
 edge-triggered IRQ

The upstream C# timer peripheral was missing the Shortcuts register
(COMPARE_CLEAR / COMPARE_STOP), BitMode support, and had a capture
task that unnecessarily cleared interrupt state.

Moving these from a Python peripheral overlay into the C# model
eliminates a Python-to-C# interop round-trip on every compare event
and every MMIO access to the Shortcuts/BitMode registers.  For
timer-heavy workloads (e.g. Zephyr kernel ticks at 32 kHz, BLE
connection-event scheduling) this removes thousands of managed
call transitions per second, reducing simulation overhead measurably.

Additionally, fix UpdateInterrupts() to use edge-triggered IRQ
signalling matching real nRF52840 hardware behaviour.  The previous
level-triggered IRQ.Set(flag) held the NVIC input high, causing
the ISR to re-enter immediately after firmware cleared the event
register and returned.  Now UpdateInterrupts() tracks the previous
IRQ state and calls IRQ.Blink() only on a 0-to-1 transition.

Specific changes:

  - Shortcuts register (0x200): implement COMPARE_CLEAR[0..N] and
    COMPARE_STOP[0..N] with in-callback clear/stop on compare match.
  - BitMode register (0x508): 8/16/24/32-bit counter width support
    via GetBitModeMask(), applied to compare writes, capture reads,
    and the Compare0..N value provider.
  - Capture task: snapshot counter value directly instead of routing
    through SetCompare(), which had the side effect of clearing the
    event flag and updating interrupts.
  - Edge-triggered IRQ: pulse via IRQ.Blink() on rising edge only.
---
 .../Timers/NRF52840_Timer.cs                  | 90 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 80 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Timers/NRF52840_Timer.cs b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Timers/NRF52840_Timer.cs
index 1fc00e9cd..cb53669bd 100644
--- a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Timers/NRF52840_Timer.cs
+++ b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Timers/NRF52840_Timer.cs
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-﻿//
+//
 // Copyright (c) 2010-2025 Antmicro
